<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="3.2" level="1">Agriculture, Animal Care, and Food</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="V" level="2">Domestic Animals</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="60" level="3">Livestock and Poultry</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="2" level="4">Disposal of Dead Poultry</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>3.2-6028</section_number>
	<catch_line>Exemptions from provisions of article</catch_line>
	<text>
		The State Veterinarian may authorize disposal of dead poultry by a method other than as provided in § 3.2-6025 or 3.2-6026 if he determines that the alternative method meets standards for disposal of dead poultry.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 3-583.5; 1962, c. 157; 1966, c. 702, § 3.1-746; 1972, c. 90; 1992, c. 101; 2008, c. 860.</history>
</law>
